  "note": "Triennial election of the rural district council (ten Co. Armagh divisions, two councillors each), polled 31 May 1911: contests in Kernan, Lurgan Rural and Portadown Rural. No party labels are printed. Polled 31 May 1911; counted on Thursday 1 June in the Lurgan Workhouse boardroom by W. J. Corner, deputy returning officer. Two seats. The old members were Gilpin and Grimshaw; Grimshaw had decided to retire but missed the date for withdrawals (Lurgan Mail, 3 June 1911, p. 5)."
